= Melen Receives the Mandate

Following Ürgüplü's failure to form a government, attention once again turns to President Sunay, who must find someone capable of resolving the continuing political crisis. MGP Chairman Turhan Feyzioğlu, having already been passed over in favor of Ürgüplü, eagerly anticipates that the responsibility will finally be entrusted to him. However, Sunay has other plans and instead gives the mandate to Ferit Melen, who has already been serving as acting Prime Minister since Erim's resignation. Unlike Feyzioğlu, whose repeated complaints about military interference, the weakened position of Parliament and the government's conduct have made his political intentions somewhat difficult for the military leadership to predict, Melen is a familiar and reliable figure. Having served as Defense Minister under Erim and already assumed responsibility for overseeing the outgoing government, Melen is someone whose views, intentions and political conduct are well understood by Sunay and the generals. With another failed attempt at forming a government behind them, the President and the military are unwilling to take further chances, leaving a disappointed Feyzioğlu to watch yet another opportunity slip through his fingers.

- @rubicon_melen_invitation: Melen invites the CHP into his government
